{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "Haha. Thanks as always. Oh, and good luck, Norimoto-kun! You got this!": "",
  "Welcome, sir!": "",
  "Yo, Norimoto-kun. I'll take a coffee, same as usual.": "",
  "Hi, Yagami-san! I'll show you to your seat.": "",
  "So. Seems like you and Miharu-chan are getting along pretty well.": "",
  "Huh!? Wh-What do you mean?": "",
  "When I came here the other day, Miharu-chan told me she's been having fun talking to you lately.": "",
  "Really!? No way! Man, I'm glad I took your advice!": "",
  "Did you go on that date yet?": "",
  "A date!? No... I have no idea where to take her.": "",
  "Maybe you could think of somewhere for me?": "",
  "Dude, why not just ask her yourself?": "",
  "On our first date? That would be super lame!": "",
  "Yeah! In this situation, a man's gotta play it smart and match the lady's preference!": "",
  "Okay, but do you even know the lady's preference to begin with?": "",
  "Nope! That's why I was gonna ask if you could find out for me.": "",
  "Wait, <font_kind=yakuza_italic>I</font_kind> have to do this? What happened to all that man talk!": "",
  "Sometimes even the bravest man needs backup! Please... Won't you be my wingman? I'll pick up your tab again!": "",
  "Fine... But don't expect too much, all right?": "",
  "You're awesome, man! Thanks!": "",
  "Oh, Yagami-san! I can't thank you enough!": "",
  "Hey, no worries.": "",
  "Welcome back, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Working hard, Norimoto-kun? I'll have the usual.": "",
  "Of course! Please, right this way!": "",
  "So, Norimoto-kun. I discovered Miharu-chan's dream date.": "",
  "...And!?": "",
  "She says she wants to go see dolphins at the aquarium.": "",
  "Ohh, I'll show her a dolphin all right! I mean... yeah! I'll go buy some aquarium tickets and ask her right away!": "",
  "You're the man, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Hey. If the date goes well, you should tell her how you feel at the end.": "",
  "...Wha!?": "",
  "Don't act so surprised. If you made it this far, you might as well share your feelings with her. Right?": "",
  "But... what if she rejects me?": "",
  "You can't just go in there thinking about rejection. Show her the real Norimoto-kun... a man that truly cares.": "",
  "O-Okay... I'll do my best...": "",
  "C'mon, what kind of response is that? Show some enthusiasm! And make sure you ask her on that date.": "",
  "...Followed by a romantic, heartfelt confession! You got all that?": "",
  "I'll do the best I can! Oh, and before I start daydreaming about all this, I'll be happy to comp your order! Gotta pay my dues.": "",
  "Haha, you really don't have to do that. Just focus on doing your best!": "",
  "R-Right! Even though I'm so nervous...": "",
  "Anyway, thank you again coming in today. And for the advice.": "",
  "Definitely. Well, I look forward to serving you again!": "",
  "Yagami-san, please find out Miharu-chan's preference for going on a date.": "",
  "Anyways, what would you like to order today?": "",
  "Yagami-san, guess what!": "",
  "Well hey, Miharu-chan, what's going on?": "",
  "Okay okay, let me show you to your seat first, and I'll tell you all about it!": "",
  "Commence checking.": "",
  "All right, Yagami-san, check this out!": "",
  "Heh, told you! So who's the lucky guy?": "",
  "Just like you predicted, I got invited to the aquarium!": "",
  "...Amazing! What a coincidence.": "",
  "Actually, it was Norimoto-kun! Can you believe it?": "",
  "(You did well, Norimoto-kun. You're on the blessed path.)": "",
  "We were talking in the back, and all of a sudden he told me he happened to get some aquarium tickets. Isn't that crazy?": "",
  "Yeah, it's your aquarium dream come true. Enjoy that date!": "",
  "Oh, it's nothing like that! We're just going as friends.": "",
  "The two of you? At an aquarium, all by yourselves? Sounds like a date to me.": "",
  "Well, when you put it like that... Geez, now I'm getting all nervous! Ohh, what should I wear...?": "",
  "Yeah... You're right. That's good advice.": "",
  "Hey now, I was just teasing. Don't think too hard about it. Just be yourself and focus on having a good time.": "",
  "Thanks for the meal, Miharu-chan. Hope you enjoy the aquarium.": "",
  "Thank youuu! ♪": "",
  "Welcome. How many in your party, sir?": "",
  "Just me.": "",
  "O-kay, party of one, please follow me.": "",
  "Have you decided what you'd like?": "",
  "You wouldn't happen to be new here, would you?": "",
  "Oh, yes! I just started part-time. My name's Miharu Shima.": "",
  "(I've heard that name before...)": "",
  "(This must be the girl Norimoto-kun's been talking about.)": "",
  "Miharu-chan, got it. I'm Yagami. I come here all the time, so it's nice to finally see a new face.": "",
  "Oh, you're a regular? Wow, it's nice to meet you!": "",
  "(Ah, to be young and in love... Guess I could help Norimoto-kun out a bit.)": "",
  "It's refreshing to see a server who's actually enthusiastic about their job. I bet you're popular with the customers.": "",
  "Haha, I wish! Unfortunately, I'm not popular inside or outside of work.": "",
  "Really? Never would've guessed. I'm sure you at least have a boyfriend, right?": "",
  "Nope! But if you know any good candidates, tell 'em I'm accepting applications. Hee-hee. ❤": "",
  "I'm sure you'll have no trouble finding a good guy... Unless you're the type who has crazy high expectations.": "",
  "Don't be silly, I'm not <font_kind=yakuza_italic>that</font_kind> picky!": "",
  "Then, just out of curiosity, on a purely platonic level... What kind of guy's your type?": "",
  "Hmm... He's gotta have a great sense of humor. And be a good conversationalist, too. Someone who can cheer me up anytime.": "",
  "...Sounds about right. Well, I hope he turns up soon.": "",
  "Me too! Pray for me, Yagami-san. Hehe.": "",
  "Well, now that you've gotten to know me a bit, would you like to place an order?": "",
  "Thank you for coming.": "",
  "Thanks for having me!": "",
  "Hey, welcome back, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Miharu-chan, how are you?": "",
  "Same as always. I'll show you to your seat now.": "",
  "So, have you found your special someone?": "",
  "Well, no. I haven't really met anyone new...": "",
  "Oh wait!": "",
  "There is this other part-time worker named Norimoto-kun that may be kinda interesting...?": "",
  "(Nice! Get in there, Norimoto-kun!)": "",
  "A fellow part-timer, you say?": "",
  "Yep. I didn't have much of an impression of him at first, but as we started talking, he actually seemed pretty cool.": "",
  "Well, isn't that a nice coincidence? Mr. Right has been here all along.": "",
  "Hmm, I wouldn't say that just yet... But it would sure be nice! Hehe.": "",
  "Now, what would you like to order?": "",
  "Thank you for coming, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Thanks for the meal. See you again.": "",
  "Oh, welcome back, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Hey there, Miharu-chan.": "",
  "Ready to be seated? Please follow me!": "",
  "Oh yeah, how's it going with that coworker you mentioned that one time?": "",
  "It's going, I guess? We do talk whenever we're on the same shift.": "",
  "But nothing's moved beyond that, huh?": "",
  "No, but at least we have fun talking. He seems genuinely interested in me, and says some pretty funny stuff.": "",
  "Okay. Have you guys, like, gone out anywhere?": "",
  "Nope, not yet.": "",
  "I see, I see. So, if he was to ask you out, let's say, what would be your ideal time together?": "",
  "You mean on a date? Hmm, I guess a normal one would be fine.": "",
  "Define normal.": "",
  "Okay... How about... Going to look at dolphins at the aquarium?": "",
  "You like dolphins, huh? They are cute.": "",
  "Aren't they!?": "",
  "They have these sparkly little eyes and adorable little flippers... Ahh, I could just die from the cuteness!": "",
  "Haha, sounds like someone really likes her marine mammals.": "",
  "Ah, all I'm trying to say is it'd be nice to go to an aquarium with a guy I really like. Dolphins or not.": "",
  "Well, I have a funny feeling you'll be able to very soon. Call me psychic or whatever.": "",
  "You're joking, right? Don't say such random things!": "",
  "Nah, I'm totally serious.": "",
  "...Honestly? I hope your prediction comes true, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Thanks for the meal, Miharu-chan. See you!": "",
  "Yagami-saaan! Welcooome!! ♪": "",
  "Wow, Miharu-chan. You look like you won the lottery.": "",
  "Hehe, really? Well, follow me and I'll tell you all about it!": "",
  "So? What's the big news? I'm assuming something good happened.": "",
  "Well, yes. See, Norimoto-kun and I... are officially together now.": "",
  "(Mission accomplished! Good going, Norimoto-kun. Now act surprised...)": "",
  "Wow, are you serious!?": "",
  "I am. On our way home from the aquarium, Norimoto-kun confessed his true feelings.": "",
  "\"Miharu-chan,\" he said. \"I see you as more than just a part-time coworker. I see you as... my full-time woman.\"": "",
  "That's... That's great! Ahahaha!": "",
  "You know, Yagami-san... It's almost like you're Cupid or something.": "",
  "Because every time I told you about my love life, it happened exactly the way you said.": "",
  "And now I have a wonderful boyfriend.": "",
  "Maybe it's all just a wonderful string of coincidences.": "",
  "You really think so? Hmm...": "",
  "Either way, I'm still glad to have met you, Yagami-san! I hope you'll always be a regular!": "",
  "You bet.": "",
  "Hehehe. May I take your order, then?": "",
  "Thanks for the meal, Miharu-chan. Best of luck to you and the new boyfriend.": "",
  "Welcome, Yagami-san. Have you tried our secret menu?": "",
  "Welcome, Yagami-san! I'm going on a trip with my boyfriend soon!": "",
  "Oh, Yagami-san, am I glad to see you!": "",
  "Glad to see you too. How's everything in the Beef Zone?": "",
  "Well, we made the prices cheaper like you suggested, and now we have many more customers!": "",
  "Is that right? That puts my mind at ease.": "",
  "But that's still not enough... At this rate, Kanrai's gonna swallow us whole!": "",
  "Can you think of any other ideas?": "",
  "Oh, Yagami-san! Welcome to the Beef Zone!": "",
  "Thanks. Has business been getting any better?": "",
  "Well, we made rice refills free like you suggested, and our expenses have gone way down!": "",
  "Good! Glad to hear it.": "",
  "Well, we did flesh out our dessert menu, and now we're rolling in sugar addicts! Which is good for business.": "",
  "Well, we made a family special like you suggested, and now we have families coming in from all over the place!": "",
  "Fantastic! That's good to know.": "",
  "Why not drop the prices a little?": "",
  "Kanrai's pretty pricey as it is, so a price drop on your end should help your place stand out. You'll be the other option.": "",
  "Why not give free refills on rice?": "",
  "Since yakiniku and rice go practically hand in hand, I think a lot of people would appreciate some rice on the house.": "",
  "Besides, wouldn't it also be better for sales if the customers filled up on rice? It's a lot cheaper than meat.": "",
  "Why not expand the dessert menu?": "",
  "That way, you'd attract more families with young kids as well as groups of girls. Helps give that menu a nice touch.": "",
  "Why not make a family special? Large parties like families tend to rack up a higher bill, which equates to more profit.": "",
  "It's true that Kanrai is a bit more on the luxury side...": "",
  "But it's also losing out on a big demographic by leaving out families. This could be your chance to corner the market!": "",
  "Wow, you really know your stuff! You sure you weren't a restaurant manager before? Feels like I've already said that.": "",
  "(Will my amateur advice really make a difference in the long run? Guess I'll find out soon enough...)": "",
  "Well, we made rice refills free like you suggested, and now\nwe have way more customers!": "",
  "Welcome to the Beef Zone! Get ready!": "",
  "Haha, ready as always. How's business these days, Kim-san?": "",
  "Well, to be honest, it's a little rough. A lot of customers have gone over to Kanrai, our main competitor.": "",
  "Well, Kanrai is pretty popular...": "",
  "Can you think of anything that would help us stay competitive?": "",
  "Not sure if I can just make it rain ideas, but I'll try.": "",
  "First off, what is Kanrai really known for in the first place?": "",
  "Let's see. It's a high-end restaurant, so it's probably more geared toward entertaining clients or fancy dates.": "",
  "And rather than making a big, fancy menu, they stick to a small selection of only the choicest meats on the market.": "",
  "They don't seem to do anything unreputable as a business, either.": "",
  "Was that information helpful at all?": "",
  "Yeah, let me think here...": "",
  "Well, we made rice refills free like you suggested, and now we have way more customers!": "",
  "But... that's still... not enough. At this rate...": "",
  "Kanrai's not gonna swallow you whole, okay? All you have to do is showcase something original... which you do have, yes?": "",
  "If we did, I would've said so earlier! And ordering a brand-new item out of the blue would only drive up costs...": "",
  "Okay, so scratch that idea. Maybe you can focus on the way you grill, or feature some kind of special sauce...": "",
  "Honestly, our grills are nothing out of the norm. And our sauce is just my grandma's old recipe.": "",
  "Can you repeat that last bit...?": "",
  "That! That's it! Kim-san, is your sauce still made the same way as your grandma's?": "",
  "Yes sir, we always use my grandma's sauce when eating yakiniku.": "",
  "The balance between the soy sauce and mirin, topped with a gentle dollop of honey is what does it.": "",
  "Then that's it! What you described to me just now... is your original, mouth-watering secret sauce!": "",
  "Ah... I see where you're going with this. Brilliant! Then I'll advertise it just like that!": "",
  "(Family-friendly yakiniku served with secret sauce, a traditional recipe from Kim-san's grandma...)": "",
  "(I think this is our best idea yet.)": "",
  "Yagami-san, we did it! My grandma's yakiniku sauce is becoming a huge hit!": "",
  "We've been getting customers left and right ever since. Business is booming now!": "",
  "Of course. You pulled out all the stops to make it happen.": "",
  "Well, we couldn't have done it without your superb advice! You have my thanks, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Ah, I didn't do much. Thank your grandma instead. ": "",
  "Yes, I should! Thanks, Grandma!": "",
  "This sauce... it's delicious. What could possibly be in it?": "",
  "Wait, is that... the manager of Kanrai?": "",
  "I heard Beef Zone's sauce was the talk of the town, so I knew I had to try it out myself...": "",
  "But this was beyond my expectations. We'll have to try even harder just to keep up with you, eh?": "",
  "Oh no, we're really nothing special.": "",
  "Nonsense! If we don't improve our own sauce, all our customers are gonna end up eating here instead!": "",
  "I'm not so sure about that, but it's quite flattering to hear from such an esteemed business as Kanrai.": "",
  "Well then, I'll be taking my leave. Let's do our best from here on out, hm?": "",
  "Yes! And thank you for entering the Beef Zone!": "",
  "Yagami-san, did you hear that just now!?": "",
  "Yeah, he really talked you up there, didn't he?": "",
  "He sure did! I got the feeling he was really impressed, so I'm all fired up now! Thank you so much, Yagami-san!": "",
  "It's something any fan would do. Keep that fire alive, Kim-san!": "",
  "Oh and by the way! As thanks, I'd like to let you eat here at a special discount price!": "",
  "You mean it!?": "",
  "Of course. You can come here and fill up any time! I'll make it cheap.": "",
  "Sounds good to me! I appreciate that.": "",
  "My pleasure. Consider it a bonus from the Beef Zone!": "",
  "Hey, Yosuke. I'm here about your case.": "",
  "Ah, here you are! I've been waiting for you, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Hm, no Tsukino today?": "",
  "R-Right. I came alone this time.": "",
  "I see. So, what's the job? It sounded pretty serious.": "",
  "Yes, it's a... delicate subject. It's the Twisted Trio again, though...": "",
  "I figured as much. I guess the third one has reared his head?": "",
  "Yeah. Do you know anything about him, Yagami-san?": "",
  "This guy is the peeping tom of the bunch...": "",
  "And the name he's been given is... Judge Creep 'n Peep.": "",
  "Yeah, I don't know why I'm surprised by these anymore.": "",
  "But it's the \"judge\" part that's got me curious. Why \"judge\"?": "",
  "He peeps in on couples at love hotels, and determines their guilt or innocence based on what he sees.": "",
  "He... what?": "",
  "He thinks of himself as some kind of authority on what should be a private matter between a man and a woman...": "",
  "And if he deems them guilty... he uploads the pics to social media.": "",
  "I can't even imagine what kind of criteria this guy has for that...": "",
  "Is it safe to say you're the victim, then? Did he catch you with your girlfriend?": "",
  "Um, no... Not exactly...": "",
  "I-I mean, I do have a girlfriend, but she's studying abroad in America right now...": "",
  "Then if you're not the victim... Don't tell me it's Tsukino?": "",
  "Y-Yes. She's been victimized yet again! He has video of her having sex with her boyfriend!": "",
  "(Huh. I guess Tsukino must have found a boyfriend since the first pervert...)": "",
  "(And that would mean this guy judged her guilty... On what grounds?)": "",
  "Tsukino is so depressed and mortified, she won't even leave the house.": "",
  "I should know the answer to this by now... But you're sure it's Judge Creep 'n Peep? Not some other guy?": "",
  "No. She saw him with her own two eyes.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "Welcome, sir!": "ยินดีต้อนรับครับท่าน!",
  "Just me.": "คนเดียว",
  "Thanks for having me!": "ขอบคุณที่รับฉันเข้าร่วมนะ!",
  "You bet.": "แน่นอนอยู่แล้ว",
  "You mean it!?": "พูดจริงเหรอครับ!?"
 }
}
